-DATASET CSV empty

--

-CASE SteinerKCoreSingleSeed
-LOAD_DYNAMIC_EXTENSION algo
-STATEMENT CREATE NODE TABLE N(id INT64 PRIMARY KEY)
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE REL TABLE E(FROM N TO N)
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (a:N{id:0}), (b:N{id:1}), (c:N{id:2}), (d:N{id:3})
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (x:N{id:1}), (y:N{id:0}) CREATE (x)-[:E]->(y)
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (x:N{id:2}), (y:N{id:0}) CREATE (x)-[:E]->(y)
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (x:N{id:3}), (y:N{id:0}) CREATE (x)-[:E]->(y)
---- ok
-STATEMENT CALL PROJECT_GRAPH('G', ['N'], ['E'])
---- ok
-LOG Star centered at 0: the whole graph is the 1-core, so seed {1} yields all nodes with k=1.
-STATEMENT CALL GDS_STEINER_K_CORE('G', [1]) RETURN node.id, community_id, coreness ORDER BY node.id
---- 4
0|0|1
1|0|1
2|0|1
3|0|1
-LOG Hub seed resolves to the same community.
-STATEMENT CALL GDS_STEINER_K_CORE('G', [0]) RETURN node.id, community_id, coreness ORDER BY node.id
---- 4
0|0|1
1|0|1
2|0|1
3|0|1
-LOG Multi-seed query in one set: {1, 2} are connected in the 1-core, same community.
-STATEMENT CALL GDS_STEINER_K_CORE('G', [1, 2]) RETURN node.id, community_id, coreness ORDER BY node.id
---- 4
0|0|1
1|0|1
2|0|1
3|0|1
-LOG Empty seed list is a binder error.
-STATEMENT CALL GDS_STEINER_K_CORE('G', []) RETURN node.id, community_id, coreness
---- error
Binder exception: GDS_STEINER_K_CORE requires at least one seed node.
-LOG Negative seeds are rejected at bind time.
-STATEMENT CALL GDS_STEINER_K_CORE('G', [-1]) RETURN node.id, community_id, coreness
---- error
Binder exception: GDS_STEINER_K_CORE seed node offsets must be non-negative.
-LOG Out-of-range seeds are rejected once the projected graph size is known.
-STATEMENT CALL GDS_STEINER_K_CORE('G', [99]) RETURN node.id, community_id, coreness
---- error
Binder exception: GDS_STEINER_K_CORE seed node offset 99 is out of range: the projected graph has 4 nodes.
